WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.261 --> 00:00:02.651
(slow upbeat music)

00:00:02.651 --> 00:00:04.792
- The first time I ever made a delivery

00:00:04.792 --> 00:00:06.875
was in the spring of 1953,

00:00:07.771 --> 00:00:11.604
and I was six months old
on my father's route.

00:00:13.171 --> 00:00:14.641
I grew up doing this.

00:00:14.641 --> 00:00:15.641
Seltzer man.

00:00:19.361 --> 00:00:21.468
My name is Walter Backerman,

00:00:21.468 --> 00:00:23.862
and I am a Seltzer Man.

00:00:23.862 --> 00:00:26.772
A Seltzer Man is the order
taker, the bottle fixer,

00:00:26.772 --> 00:00:28.590
the driver, the deliverer,

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:30.062
the salesman.

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:31.969
You're everything rolled into one.

00:00:31.969 --> 00:00:34.910
If people ask you what it is
about the seltzer business

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:38.362
that makes you wanna continue doing it,

00:00:38.362 --> 00:00:39.779
you hold that seltzer bottle

00:00:39.779 --> 00:00:41.449
and you hold history.

00:00:41.449 --> 00:00:42.579
You hold memories.

00:00:42.579 --> 00:00:44.950
You hold an object of beauty.

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:45.950
That's 1871.

00:00:47.289 --> 00:00:48.539
It still works.

00:00:51.310 --> 00:00:54.910
- Without these bottles,
this business doesn't exist.

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:58.990
This machine is a Barnett &amp;
Foster siphon filling machine.

00:00:58.990 --> 00:01:02.329
I think it was made in
London, early 1900s.

00:01:02.329 --> 00:01:04.390
It's a six siphon grade filling machine.

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:06.150
It goes around through the carousel

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:08.118
and only one bottle goes in at a time.

00:01:08.118 --> 00:01:10.489
So it's a lot of work.

00:01:10.489 --> 00:01:12.872
The reason this is a better seltzer

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:16.357
is because there's nothing
else in this seltzer

00:01:16.357 --> 00:01:18.910
other than New York City tap water,

00:01:18.910 --> 00:01:20.758
which is triple-filtered
through sand, charcoal,

00:01:20.758 --> 00:01:22.258
and paper, and CO2.

00:01:23.889 --> 00:01:26.579
- Fortunately, as long
as the machine is fixed

00:01:26.579 --> 00:01:28.070
and I have a place to fill,

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:30.358
I can't see any reason why this business

00:01:30.358 --> 00:01:33.158
should be a nail in the coffin situation

00:01:33.158 --> 00:01:34.169
where it's over.

00:01:34.169 --> 00:01:36.611
It won't be over till the
last bottle of seltzer

00:01:36.611 --> 00:01:40.444
is squirted, and I don't
see that anytime soon.

